{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR Client.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR Client.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"signal r client signal r client","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR Client.md","fileName":"SignalR Client.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SignalR Client","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:52\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Real-Time Web Communication]] [[Azure SignalR Service Applications]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Real-Time Web Communication","Azure SignalR Service Applications","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andreact.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR Client.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR Client.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"signal r client signal r client","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SignalR Client.md","fileName":"SignalR Client.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SignalR Client","heading":"SignalR Client","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A SignalR client is the browser-side library and configuration that connect a React application to an ASP.NET Core hub. It builds the connection, attaches callbacks to server message names, and starts or stops communication.\n\nThe callback converts the received payload into a state update that React can render. Cross-origin configuration must permit the connection when the client and API run at different origins.\n\nThe book's browser client installs the JavaScript SignalR library, builds a connection to the mapped chat route, and registers functions for server-sent events before starting the connection. Its handlers turn the hub's messages into visible chat state and archive feedback.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Real-Time Web Communication","Azure SignalR Service Applications","c8andnetcore30projectsus